</b>​</div><i>Here for It All</i> is the sixteenth studio album by American singer-songwriter <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariah_Carey" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Mariah Carey</a>. The album was released on September 26, 2025, through her imprint Mariah, and media company <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamma_(media_company)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Gamma</a>. It features collaborations with <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anderson_.Paak" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Anderson .Paak</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kehlani" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Kehlani</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shenseea" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Shenseea</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Clark_Sisters" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">The Clark Sisters</a>, and is primarily an <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contemporary_R%26B" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">R&amp;B</a> album, with elements of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">pop</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hip-hop" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">hip-hop</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">soul</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disco" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">disco</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funk" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">funk</a>, and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gospel_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">gospel</a>. The album was preceded by the release of two singles: the lead single "<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_Dangerous" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Type Dangerous</a>", was released on June 5, 2025, followed by "<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sugar_Sweet" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Sugar Sweet</a>" on July 25.<b><br>
</b><br>
